.TH ACCLORITE 1 "September 2026" "Acclorite 0.3.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
acclorite \- local-first deterministic Linux tool discovery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acclorite
.RI [ options ] " query ..."
.br
.B acclorite
.RI [ --json ] " doctor"
.br
.B acclorite --reindex
.br
.B acclorite
.RI [ --json ] " --capabilities"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Acclorite turns task-oriented Linux questions into ranked tool recommendations using local executable, manual, desktop, package, and optional local guidance metadata. The normal runtime is deterministic, non-interactive, local-first, and offline.
.PP
Human terminal output includes the interpreted query frame, the primary candidate, local guidance, confidence, and clarifications when the query is ambiguous. Machine clients should use
.B --json
and
.B --capabilities
rather than parsing human output.
.PP
On Fedora/RHEL-family systems, the DNF package backend prefers dnf5 and falls back to dnf. All DNF repository queries are invoked with --cacheonly; Acclorite does not refresh repository metadata or perform package transactions.
.PP
On openSUSE-family systems, the Zypper package backend uses machine-readable XML search with --no-refresh and a bundled read-only configuration that disables the optional zypper-search-packages extended lookup. Acclorite does not refresh repositories or perform Zypper transactions.
.PP
On Void Linux, the XBPS backend searches synchronized on-disk repository indexes with xbps-query and never enables -M/--memory-sync. Acclorite never invokes xbps-install or another XBPS transaction frontend; xbps-uhelper is used only to decode package-version metadata.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Emit stable machine-readable JSON for search or Doctor.
.TP
.B --explain-ranking
Include ranking evidence and score adjustments in human or JSON search output.
.TP
.B --profile
Include internal search-stage timings.
.TP
.B --capabilities
Emit the machine capability document, including schema versions and stable exit codes.
.TP
.B --reindex
Rebuild the local persistent search index. Rebuilds are staged and validated before atomically replacing the live index; a failed rebuild preserves the previous usable snapshot.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show help.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Print the Acclorite version.
.TP
.B --
Stop option parsing; remaining arguments are query text.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Inspect local readiness without modifying the system. Doctor never refreshes package databases, installs software, rebuilds the index, or updates TLDR metadata.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/acclorite/index.db
Persistent local FTS index. Defaults to
.I ~/.cache/acclorite/index.db
when XDG_CACHE_HOME is unset.
.TP
.I /usr/share/acclorite/curated-guidance.tsv
Typical system location of the bundled curated offline guidance corpus. Acclorite also supports relocated installation prefixes by resolving this data relative to its executable.
.TP
.I /usr/share/acclorite/zypper-readonly.conf
Bundled query-only Zypper policy used by the openSUSE backend. It disables the optional extended search-packages hook so normal Acclorite repository discovery remains local.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI styling in interactive human output.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Override the base directory used for Acclorite caches.
.TP
.B ACCLORITE_CURATED_GUIDANCE
Explicitly override the curated guidance TSV. Override data is marked with local override provenance rather than Acclorite-project provenance.
.TP
.B ACCLORITE_OS_RELEASE
Override the path used for distro-family detection instead of /etc/os-release. This is intended for controlled environments, tests, chroots, and packaging validation rather than ordinary user configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Valid search completed but produced no result.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid invocation or CLI usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Operational failure.
.TP
.B 4
Doctor completed and found a fundamental broken-state diagnostic.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
acclorite "search text inside files"
acclorite "what is rg"
acclorite "where is ssh config"
acclorite "difference between rg and grep"
acclorite doctor
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The installed Acclorite documentation and machine-interface contract under the package documentation directory.
